<title>SINGAPORE: Wee Poh up over 70 pct from IPO at debut.</title>
<headline>Wee Poh up over 70 pct from IPO at debut.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in newly-listed infrastructure company Wee Poh Holdings Ltd jumped more than 70 percent from its initial public offer (IPO) price to a high of Singapore $0.785 in the first three minutes of trading on Monday.  </p>
<p>The share, which was offered at 45 cents at its IPO, then put on another half cent to reach a high of S$0.79 before sliding back to S$0.765 by 0115 GMT.</p>
<p>Wee Poh's IPO of 24.8 million shares, which included a placement tranche of 6.2 million shares, was 101 times subscribed.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
